# =============================================================================
# Computational-Immuno-oncology — .gitignore
# =============================================================================
# This repo holds TEACHING MATERIAL: documents, scripts, notebooks, small
# example data. It must NOT hold analysis outputs, sequencing data, or secrets.
#
# Rule of thumb: if it can be regenerated by running a script, it does not
# belong in git.  Students keep run outputs under $HOME, never in this repo.
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Secrets & credentials  (see skill: github-safe-push)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
*api*key*
*apikey*
*secret*
*credential*
*password*
*passwd*
*token*
*.env
*.env.*
.env.local
.env.*.local
*.local
*.local.*
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.crt
*.cer
*.der
*.csr
*.p8
*.ppk
*.local.jsonc
*.local.json
*.local.yaml
*.local.yml
*.local.toml
config.local.*
settings.local.*
# allow committed templates
!*.example
!*.template
!*.dist
!*.sample

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. Sequencing data — never in git (huge + often controlled-access)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.fastq
*.fastq.gz
*.fq
*.fq.gz
*.sra
*.fast5
*.pod5
*.bam
*.bai
*.cram
*.crai
*.sam
*.sai
*.bed.gz
*.bed.gz.tbi
*.vcf
*.vcf.gz
*.vcf.gz.tbi
*.g.vcf
*.g.vcf.idx
*.bcf
*.gvcf
*.idat
*.cel
# small teaching fixtures may be force-added with: git add -f <path>
!WES/ref/*.bed
!WES/ref/*.fa
!WES/ref/*.fasta

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. Pipeline run outputs
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
wes_run_cluster_*/
wes_run_*/
run_*/
*.clean.fq.gz
*.clean.fastq.gz
*.flagstat.txt
*.markdup.bam
*.markdup.bam.bai
*_sorted.bam
*_sorted.bam.bai
*_markdup_metrics.txt
*.recal_data.table
*.recal
*.tranches
*.plots.R
*.avinput
*_multianno.txt
*.hg38_multianno.txt
*.cnn
*.cnr
*.cns
*.call.cns
*.seg
*.targetcoverage.cnn
*.antitargetcoverage.cnn
*.reference.cnn
*scatter*.png
*diagram*.pdf
*.fastp.html
*.fastp.json
*.multiqc.html
*.multiqc_data/
*.vcf.stats
f1r2.tar.gz
orientation_model.tar.gz
tmb.txt
coverage_summary.txt

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 4. Logs & job scheduler output
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
logs/
log/
slurm-*.out
slurm-*.err
*.out
*.err
core.*

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 5. Python
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
develop-eggs/
downloads/
wheels/
pip-wheel-metadata/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
coverage.xml
htmlcov/
Rplots.pdf
.Rhistory
.RData
.Rproj.user/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 6. Editors & OS
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
*.sublime-*
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 7. Temp & backups
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
tmp/
temp/
.cache/
*.tmp
*.bak
*.backup
*.bkp
*.old
*.orig
*~
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 8. WES/results — curated analysis results (EXPLICIT exception, 2026-09-21)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deliberate user decision: the curated two-run analysis outputs under
# WES/results ARE versioned (small evidence files, reviewed selection,
# NO raw data — see WES/results/README.md and WES_results_guide.md section 5).
# Re-allow everything the general output rules above ignore, under this tree:
!WES/results/**

# Safety net: raw data & regeneration-heavy binaries never enter the repo,
# not even via the exception above:
WES/results/**/*.bam
WES/results/**/*.bai
WES/results/**/*.sam
WES/results/**/*.cram
WES/results/**/*.fastq
WES/results/**/*.fastq.gz
WES/results/**/*.fq
WES/results/**/*.fq.gz
WES/results/**/*.g.vcf
WES/results/**/*.g.vcf.idx
WES/results/**/*.g.vcf.gz
WES/results/**/f1r2.tar.gz
WES/results/**/orientation_model.tar.gz
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 9. RNA-seq/results — curated analysis results (EXPLICIT exception, 2026-10-09)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Same deliberate policy as section 8 (WES/results): the curated two-round
# RNA-seq analysis outputs ARE versioned (QC reports, metrics, logs, scripts,
# salmon quant.sf of the quasi mode as .gz, R PDFs — see
# RNA-seq/ref/RNA_seq_tutorial_corrected.md section 14 and
# RNA-seq/ref/RNA_seq_results_guide.md). NO raw data.
!RNA-seq/results/**

# Safety net (mirrors section 8): raw data & heavy intermediates never enter,
# not even via the exception above:
RNA-seq/results/**/*.bam
RNA-seq/results/**/*.bai
RNA-seq/results/**/*.sam
RNA-seq/results/**/*.cram
RNA-seq/results/**/*.fastq
RNA-seq/results/**/*.fastq.gz
RNA-seq/results/**/*.fq
RNA-seq/results/**/*.fq.gz
RNA-seq/results/**/*.g.vcf
RNA-seq/results/**/*.g.vcf.idx
RNA-seq/results/**/*.g.vcf.gz
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 10. RNA-seq-application/results — curated analysis results (EXPLICIT exception, 2026-10-12)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Same deliberate policy as sections 8 (WES/results) and 9 (RNA-seq/results):
# the Lesson-3 downstream analysis outputs ARE versioned (correlation/survival/
# immune-infiltration/TIDE figures, deconvolution result tables, TIDE output,
# scripts and logs — see RNA-seq-application/ref/RNA_seq_application_corrected.md
# and RNA_seq_application_results_guide.md). NO raw data.
!RNA-seq-application/results/**

# Safety net (mirrors sections 8/9): raw data & heavy intermediates never enter,
# not even via the exception above. Expression/follow-up files live on the shared
# read-only path /lustre1/share/rnaimmune/ and are never copied into the repo.
RNA-seq-application/results/**/*.bam
RNA-seq-application/results/**/*.bai
RNA-seq-application/results/**/*.sam
RNA-seq-application/results/**/*.cram
RNA-seq-application/results/**/*.fastq
RNA-seq-application/results/**/*.fastq.gz
RNA-seq-application/results/**/*.fq
RNA-seq-application/results/**/*.fq.gz
RNA-seq-application/results/**/*.g.vcf
RNA-seq-application/results/**/*.g.vcf.idx
RNA-seq-application/results/**/*.g.vcf.gz
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 11. TBCR-analysis/results — curated analysis results (EXPLICIT exception, 2026-10-19)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Same deliberate policy as sections 8 (WES/results), 9 (RNA-seq/results) and
# 10 (RNA-seq-application/results): the Lesson-4 TCR/BCR repertoire analysis
# outputs ARE versioned (clonotype/gene-usage/CDR3-length figures, the 375-sample
# diversity CSV of the as-written run, the corrected-pass CSVs and figures,
# scripts and logs — see TBCR-analysis/ref/TBCR_analysis_corrected.md and
# TBCR_analysis_results_guide.md). NO raw data.
!TBCR-analysis/results/**

# Safety net (mirrors sections 8/9/10): raw data & heavy intermediates never
# enter, not even via the exception above. TRUST3 outputs (cdr3.out, final.out,
# raw.out, assembled_reads.fa, ...) live on the shared read-only path
# /lustre1/share/airr/data/ and are never copied into the repo.
TBCR-analysis/results/**/*.bam
TBCR-analysis/results/**/*.bai
TBCR-analysis/results/**/*.sam
TBCR-analysis/results/**/*.cram
TBCR-analysis/results/**/*.fastq
TBCR-analysis/results/**/*.fastq.gz
TBCR-analysis/results/**/*.fq
TBCR-analysis/results/**/*.fq.gz
TBCR-analysis/results/**/*.fa
TBCR-analysis/results/**/*.fasta
TBCR-analysis/results/**/*.out
TBCR-analysis/results/**/*.g.vcf
TBCR-analysis/results/**/*.g.vcf.idx
TBCR-analysis/results/**/*.g.vcf.gz

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 12. scRNA-seq/results — curated analysis results (EXPLICIT exception, 2026-10-26)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Same deliberate policy as sections 8-11: the Lesson-5 single-cell outputs ARE
# versioned (QC/PCA/clustering/annotation/DEG/integration figures, marker tables,
# cross-tool correspondence tables, the figure-comparison tables against the 28
# course reference PNGs, per-cell run logs, scripts and the pbmc3k.h5ad deliverable
# of Part 8 — see scRNA-seq/ref/scRNA_seq_analyze_corrected.md and
# scRNA_seq_analyze_results_guide.md). NO raw data.
!scRNA-seq/results/**

# Documentation figures live in <module>/ref/figures/ and must escape sec.3's
# *scatter*.png rule (the scanpy QC scatters are named ...scatter...png) and
# *diagram*.pdf.
!*/ref/figures/**

# The course's own 28 reference PNGs (scRNA-seq/*.png) are archived at module root,
# so two of them must escape sec.3's *scatter*.png rule as well.
!scRNA-seq/*.png

# This exception has to win over two earlier generic rules:
#   * sec.3  *scatter*.png  — the scanpy QC scatter plots are named
#     scatterscanpy_scatter_*.png (scanpy concatenates its own base name);
#   * sec.4  *.log          — the console captures are kept as *.txt instead, so
#     only the per-cell logs (*_cell_log.txt) and summaries are versioned.
!scRNA-seq/results/**/*.png
!scRNA-seq/results/**/*.csv
!scRNA-seq/results/**/*.tsv
!scRNA-seq/results/**/*.md

# Safety net (mirrors sections 8-11): no raw data, no large binary objects.
# pbmc3k.h5ad is a deliberate exception (20 MB, the Part-8 deliverable);
# the 274 MB pbmc3k_final.rds and the 121 MB merged harmonised object stay out
# and are regenerated by one saveRDS() line each.
scRNA-seq/results/**/*.bam
scRNA-seq/results/**/*.bai
scRNA-seq/results/**/*.sam
scRNA-seq/results/**/*.cram
scRNA-seq/results/**/*.fastq
scRNA-seq/results/**/*.fastq.gz
scRNA-seq/results/**/*.fq
scRNA-seq/results/**/*.fq.gz
scRNA-seq/results/**/*.rds
scRNA-seq/results/**/*.RData
scRNA-seq/results/**/*.mtx
scRNA-seq/results/**/barcodes.tsv
scRNA-seq/results/**/genes.tsv

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 13. scRNA-seq-scVelo/results — curated analysis results (EXPLICIT exception, 2026-11-04)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Same deliberate policy as sections 8-12: the Lesson-6 RNA-velocity outputs ARE versioned
# (the tutorial's 11 figures from the as-written run, the corrected-pass figures including the
# dynamical/EM model and the latent-time panels, per-cell velocity / latent-time / confidence
# tables, the sensitivity tables for the tutorial's unexplained defaults, the figure-comparison
# TSV against the 11 course reference PNGs, and the console logs). NO raw data and NO AnnData
# object: the 162 MB .h5ad is regenerated by one adata.write() line, see
# scRNA-seq-scVelo/ref/scVelo_analysis_results_guide.md.
!scRNA-seq-scVelo/results/**

# Safety net (mirrors sections 8-12): no raw data, no big binary objects. The course input
# 52 MB endocrinogenesis_day15.h5ad stays out of git (it ships with the course under
# /lustre1/share/scRNA-advancedTopics/data/Pancreas/).
scRNA-seq-scVelo/results/**/*.h5ad
scRNA-seq-scVelo/results/**/*.h5
scRNA-seq-scVelo/results/**/*.loom
scRNA-seq-scVelo/results/**/*.bam
scRNA-seq-scVelo/results/**/*.bai
scRNA-seq-scVelo/results/**/*.sam
scRNA-seq-scVelo/results/**/*.cram
scRNA-seq-scVelo/results/**/*.fastq
scRNA-seq-scVelo/results/**/*.fastq.gz
scRNA-seq-scVelo/results/**/*.fq
scRNA-seq-scVelo/results/**/*.fq.gz

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 14. scRNA-seq-application-dynamo/results — curated analysis results (EXPLICIT exception, 2026-11-09)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Same deliberate policy as sections 8-13: the Lesson-7 (Dynamo vector field) outputs ARE versioned
# (the tutorial's 6 as-written figures plus the 3 Jacobian panels it only displays inline, the
# per-cell speed/divergence/acceleration/curl/ddhodge-potential table, the per-cluster means and
# Kruskal-Wallis/Mann-Whitney tests, the exported 8x8 state-graph matrices, the gene-level Jacobian
# tensors and pair tables, the 925-row GO enrichment table, the figure-comparison TSV against BOTH
# teacher reference sets, and the console log). NO raw data and NO AnnData object: the 3.3 GB
# dynamo_pancreas_final.h5ad is regenerated by the scripts, and the course input
# endocrinogenesis_day15.h5ad stays on the shared read-only path.
!scRNA-seq-application-dynamo/results/**

# Safety net (mirrors sections 8-13): no raw data, no big binary objects.
scRNA-seq-application-dynamo/results/**/*.h5ad
scRNA-seq-application-dynamo/results/**/*.h5
scRNA-seq-application-dynamo/results/**/*.loom
scRNA-seq-application-dynamo/results/**/*.bam
scRNA-seq-application-dynamo/results/**/*.bai
scRNA-seq-application-dynamo/results/**/*.sam
scRNA-seq-application-dynamo/results/**/*.cram
scRNA-seq-application-dynamo/results/**/*.fastq
scRNA-seq-application-dynamo/results/**/*.fastq.gz
scRNA-seq-application-dynamo/results/**/*.fq
scRNA-seq-application-dynamo/results/**/*.fq.gz
scRNA-seq-application-dynamo/results/**/*.vcf

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 15. scRNA-seq-cellchat/results — curated analysis results (EXPLICIT exception, 2026-11-10)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Same deliberate policy as sections 8-14: the Lesson-8 (CellphoneDB) outputs ARE versioned
# (the tutorial's 4 simple-scoring tables and 8 statistical tables, the 3 analysis figures it
# renders, the C1 PV panel in both the 24-column typo form and the 36-column corrected form, the
# threshold sweep, the query results, the 9x9 significant-interaction matrix and the row-order
# audit that catches the id/position join trap, the DEG-branch tables and dot plots the tutorial
# switches off, the figure-comparison TSV against BOTH teacher reference sets, and every console
# log). NO raw data and NO AnnData object: normalised_log_counts.h5ad stays on the shared
# read-only /lustre1 path.
!scRNA-seq-cellchat/results/**

# Safety net (mirrors sections 8-14): no raw data, no big binary objects.
scRNA-seq-cellchat/results/**/*.h5ad
scRNA-seq-cellchat/results/**/*.h5
scRNA-seq-cellchat/results/**/*.loom
scRNA-seq-cellchat/results/**/*.bam
